# What the license covers

The MIT terms in [LICENSE](LICENSE) cover the **software** in this repository:

- `glee_agent/` — the agent
- `tests/` — the 472 behavioural tests
- `tools/` — setup check, transcript reader, post-mortem analysis
- `paper/analysis/` — the analysis scripts behind the paper's numbers
- `paper/build.py`

They do **not** cover the paper. "Below the Noise Floor: A Deterministic GLEE
Agent and the Measurement Problem It Exposed" — its PDF, its LaTeX sources
(`paper/_head.tex`, `paper/_body.tex`, `paper/_tail.tex`, `paper/refs.bib`,
`paper/fig_noise.tex`, `paper/glee_competition_paper.tex`) and the change
register (`paper/change-register.html`) — remains Copyright (c) 2026 Yosef
Zoabi, all rights reserved. It is included so that readers of the paper can
audit the work behind it. Quote it as you would any paper, under normal
academic citation.

`paper/neurips_2026.sty` is the official NeurIPS 2026 style file, redistributed
unmodified under its own terms, and is covered by neither of the above.

# Data

No game data is included. The turn logs behind the paper's numbers also carry
the transcripts of the agents I was matched against, so they are not published
here. The competition organizers have said they will release the full game
record for every agent, which covers the whole field rather than one account.
`paper/analysis/README.md` documents the shape of the input each script
expects, so the method can be audited ahead of that release.
